{"archetypes":[{"name":"token-pricing","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff migrates token-cost accounting into Python while preserving shell pricing authority and mixed bucket behavior.","prompt_body":"Investigate the report_tokens_cost, report_tokens_render, and related model changes for pricing correctness. Check that scripts/token-cost.sh remains authoritative for headline totals, per-vendor bucket versus blended arguments are preserved, env rate overrides reach the child process, and fallback estimates are visibly non-authoritative. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"cli-bridge","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The live /report-tokens entrypoint changes from a large shell script to a quiet-mode shell wrapper plus Python CLI.","prompt_body":"Investigate the run-analysis.sh wrapper and report_tokens_cli integration boundary. Check argv and environment compatibility for --skill, --no-issue, --no-plot, removed --plot-from behavior, exit codes, stdout/stderr contracts, and quiet-mode file descriptor restoration. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"issue-posting","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"Report issue creation now depends on Python redaction, byte trimming, gh invocation, and optional sensitive spend fields.","prompt_body":"Investigate report_tokens_issue, gh.issue_create, redact updates, and issue-related docs/tests. Check final-byte-size trimming after redaction, immutable truncation notices, repo slug handling, surfaced gh failures, absence of raw JSON blocks, and protection against leaking tmp paths or actual spend by default. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"log-scan","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The scanner defines which larch-log runs are included, skipped, priced, and categorized for each skill.","prompt_body":"Investigate report_tokens_scan and the RunRecord construction path. Check fail-soft behavior for malformed manifests, timing, run-params, and token reports; verify missing pricing data is skipped rather than zeroed; and confirm implement includes unknown workflow runs while design preserves SIMPLE/HARD views. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"plot-boundary","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Matplotlib is intentionally isolated outside python/ to preserve the stdlib-only runtime invariant.","prompt_body":"Investigate report_tokens_plot, plot-cost-over-time.py, the plot schema docs, and stdlib-only tests. Check that matplotlib imports remain outside scanned python modules, subprocess invocation uses the runner seam and sys.executable, MPLCONFIGDIR and persistent output directories are handled correctly, and plot failures degrade gracefully. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"shell-parity","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff also adds or changes Python ports and parity tests around ship, merge, finalize, and run-log surfaces.","prompt_body":"Investigate the Python ship, merge, finalize, run_context, and run_logs changes against their shell-facing contracts. Check that new shared context handling, restore/finalize behavior, merge paths, and relevant-check routing preserve existing workflow semantics and do not introduce unintended live runtime changes outside the report-tokens plan. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
